      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 3 y^{2}&=16 x^{2} + 256\\\\- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 256&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 256$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 256)\\,i-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 256)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 6 y)\\,i-(- 32 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\32 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=4x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=4x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}3(4x)^{2}+8x(4x)-16x^{2}-256&=0\\\\64x^{2}-256&=0\\\\x^{2}&=4\\\\x&=\\pm 2\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(2,8)$ and $(-2,-8)$."
    },
